<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antalas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 530–548</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antalas was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> chief who ruled a principality around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gafsa">Capsa</a> (Gafsa) in southern Byzacena, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, in the 6th century. Around 530 he defeated a Vandal army sent by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hilderic">Hilderic</a>. He allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> after their conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> but rebelled in 544, when his forces killed the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cillium">Cillium</a>, before submitting to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-troglita">John Troglita</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/procopius">Procopius</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corippus">Corippus</a> record his career.</p></div>
